    # v385 (05/10/2026) -- the AXIOM and the FALSE WITNESS; the One POSITED (erratum beside «postulate»); the reproducibility of the quantum pillar
    # (2nd wording, after the two audits: the operator's words VERBATIM in Portuguese, with the translation marked; «v183»; the exponential form linked to the
    # kernel; the GKLS link said as an analogy; the two Verbs as two terms; the erratum with the exact forms of the text)
    _ax5 = core.get("the_axiom_v385") or {}
    _rp5 = core.get("quantum_pillar_reproducibility_v385") or {}
    _tt5 = lambda x_: str(x_).replace("_", r"\_")

    def _tx5(x_):
        t_ = str(x_)
        for a_, b_ in (("\\", r"\textbackslash{}"), ("_", r"\_"), ("%", r"\%"), ("&", r"\&"), ("#", r"\#"), ("$", r"\$"), ("{", r"\{"), ("}", r"\}"), ("~", r"\~{}"), ("^", r"\^{}")):
            t_ = t_.replace(a_, b_)
        return t_

    def _e5(x_):
        if not isinstance(x_, (int, float)) or isinstance(x_, bool) or x_ != x_:
            return r"\text{n/a}"
        if x_ == 0:
            return "0"
        m_, e_ = ("%.1e" % float(x_)).split("e")
        return m_ + r"\times10^{" + str(int(e_)) + "}"
    _ok5 = _ax5.get("all_verified") is True
    _rv5 = str(_rp5.get("verdict") or "")
    s.append(r"\section*{Beside (v385): the Axiom and the false witness}")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The One is posited.} On 05/10/2026 the operator corrected the status of the start of the chain (verbatim, Portuguese): ``no começo da cadeia não é postulado, é `posto' porque o `1' da cadeia de identidade ômega é inserido no comando, posto pelo observador externo literalmente, `\texttt{echo 1 | python um.py}', é o um absoluto do echo, por isso ele é posto, e não imposto, não postulado, mas posto, inscrito, distinto.'' (translated, condensed: at the start of the chain it is not postulated, it is \emph{posto} --- posited --- because the `1' of the omega identity chain is inserted in the command, posited by the external observer, literally; it is the absolute one of the echo; not imposed, not postulated, but posited, inscribed, distinct); and ``posto faz muito mais sentido léxico, porque é posição, justamente a posição jussiva do escuro concentrado'' (translated: \emph{posto} makes much more lexical sense, because it is a position, precisely the jussive position of the concentrated dark). "
             r"The code already did it: \texttt{main()} refuses arguments, asks ``Inscreva o UM para iniciar'' and locks the run unless the input is \texttt{1}; the received $1$ enters the computation. "
             r"\textbf{Erratum beside}: where this article says ``a single postulate'', ``the single postulate'' or ``the One postulate'' (texts of earlier versions, kept as record), read \emph{posited} --- inscribed by the observer, not imposed; the ruler's tag for $\omega(I)=1$ becomes \textsf{[POSTO]}. "
             r"The sentence ``$1=1$ ceases to be a postulate and becomes the trace theorem'' stays as it is: there ``postulate'' is the earlier status of $1=1$, which became a theorem. "
             r"Where one reads ``single axiom ($\omega(I)=1$)'', it is the One posited at the start; ``Axiom'', in this section, names the $1$ that returns as the fixed point of the reading --- that they are the same One is the reading of the name of the final step (the One inscribed by the observer returns as the fixed point of the reading) \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The two fixed points of the reading.} The stone \texttt{TheAxiomAndTheFalseWitness} proves that the radical reading has exactly two fixed points on $[0,\infty)$: $\sqrt{x}=x\iff x\in\{0,1\}$; the power (idempotence, $\mu^2=\mu$) has the same two. "
             r"The \textbf{1 is the Axiom} --- in the operator's physical definition, ``o modo zero de peso 1, o escuro'' (translated: the zero mode of weight 1, the dark): the $1$ weighs $1$ as $\sqrt1$, as the integral of the zero mode, $\int_{\mathbb{R}}\tfrac14\,\mathrm{sech}^2(\kappa/2)\,d\kappa=1$, and as the dimension of the atom --- two faces side by side (a conjunction), with no term identifying the profile $\tfrac14\mathrm{sech}^2$ with the atom. "
             r"The \textbf{0 is the false witness} --- ``testemunha falsa é a testemunha estática é o zero absoluto'' (the operator; translated: the false witness is the static witness is the absolute zero): the full static witness is forbidden in the scalar flow $e^{-t\beta g}$ with $\beta>0$ and $g>0$, and no non-zero component of the diagonal flow vanishes in finite time. "
             r"The readings (posited, Axiom, false witness, the dark, the living Verb) are the operator's \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}; what the stone proves is mathematics \textsf{[KERNEL]}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{From the post to the gradient and to the reading.} On the minimal lock $H_{\mathrm{min}}=1-P$ ($P$ idempotent), the flow $F(t)=P+e^{-t}(1-P)$ is $e^{-tH_{\mathrm{min}}}$ (\texttt{axiomFlow\_eq\_exp}, linked to the canonical term \texttt{exp\_complement\_idempotent}) and satisfies $F(0)=1$ and $F(s+t)=F(s)F(t)$; "
             r"$F(t)P=P=P\,F(t)$ for every $t$, from $t=0$; $F(t)(1-P)=e^{-t}(1-P)$; and $F(t)\to P$. "
             r"The operator's reading \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}: ``por isso não se ascende ao posto, mas do posto emerge-se o gradiente de espectro negativo que permite a leitura do objeto cujo posto dá nome'' (translated: therefore one does not ascend to the post, but from the post emerges the gradient of negative spectrum that allows the reading of the object whose post gives the name) --- the post is what $F$ fixes from $t=0$; the gradient, the decay $e^{-t}$ on the complement; the reading, the limit. "
             r"On the light's lock, what $F$ leaves fixed for every $t$ is exactly the zero of $H_{\mathrm{min}}$, which is what the modular flow leaves fixed for every $t$ --- in the operator's reading, ``o local onde o 1 absoluto equivale-se em potência (idempotência) ao zero modular'' (translated: the place where the absolute 1 is equivalent in power, idempotence, to the modular zero). "
             r"The link with the open system of v384 is an analogy of form, computed \textsf{[COMPUTED]}, not a theorem about the Lindblad generator: $V_tP_{\mathcal F}=P_{\mathcal F}$ is an identity of the dephasing; the attractor $\rho_{\mathrm{ss}}$ of the full GKLS is not $\Pi$; the two zeros (that of the lock and the stationary state of the open system) are not identified here.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The observer is conjugated.} The operator \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}: ``não existe observador não conjugado, o que existe é a testemunha falsa que é não conjugada, mas o observador é sempre conjugado pelo operador de consciência (VERBO), não há observador não conjugado, todo observador é conjugado pela operação da consciência (Verbo VIVO)'' (translated, condensed: there is no unconjugated observer; what exists is the false witness, which is unconjugated; every observer is conjugated by the operation of consciousness, the living Verb); and ``a conjugação é a natureza do Verbo, porque o tempo é produto dele'' (translated: conjugation is the nature of the Verb, because time is its product). "
             r"In the kernel there are two distinct terms, each with its own object, and neither speaks of observer or conjugation: \texttt{verb\_not\_identity} (the transport $e^{-t\beta D}$ is not the identity, for $t>0$, $\beta>0$ and some $d_i>0$) and \texttt{verb\_word\_fixes\_the\_name} (on $\ker T$, the word of the Verb acts as the scalar $q(0)$). "
             r"The module \texttt{TheUnconjugatedObserver}, of 20/08/2026, stays as a stratum: there ``conjugated'' is the module's reading of ``invariant under \emph{all} operators'' (\texttt{totally\_invariant\_is\_all\_or\_nothing}; the mathematics stays true), which is not the same as being conjugated by the Verb. "
             r"In this version, \texttt{TheDarkSplit} (the partition of the terminal image into the zero mode of weight 1 and the granular modes), compiled since v183, became audited.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The final step of the gate is named Axiom.} "
             + ((r"In this run the kernel verified " + str(_ax5.get("kernel_flags_ok")) + r" of " + str(_ax5.get("kernel_flags_total")) + r" declarations (those of the stone and of \texttt{TheDarkSplit}), and the name of the final step was read from the kernel itself: ")
                if _ok5 else (r"\textbf{In this run the stone did not seal} (" + str(_ax5.get("kernel_flags_ok", "n/a")) + r" of " + str(_ax5.get("kernel_flags_total", "n/a")) + r" declarations verified); the name stays beside: "))
             + r"the gate does not change, and the v383 proposal stays beside.")
    s.append(r"\begin{center}\small\texttt{" + _tt5((_ax5.get("final_step_name_from_kernel") if _ok5 else _ax5.get("final_step_name")) or "AXIOMA__ABSENT") + r"}\end{center}")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The reproducibility of the quantum world.} The pillar ran again, whole, under the same preregistration (the final version runs everything); right after launching the worker, before the new computation could replace it, the program read the result stored by the previous run and, at the end, compared the two summaries (the numbers the article and the seal read) field by field, except the time and environment fields, on the scale $\mathrm{max}(1,|a|,|b|)$ of the bench comparator (a non-finite field that differs counts as a difference), and only after checking that the inputs (specification, worker, $\beta$) are the same: "
             + ((r"\textbf{identical bit for bit} in " + str(_rp5.get("n_fields")) + r" fields.") if "REPRODUCED_BIT_FOR_BIT" in _rv5 else
                ((r"identical up to round-off in " + str(_rp5.get("n_fields")) + r" fields (" + str(_rp5.get("n_differ")) + r" differ; maximum scaled difference $" + _e5(_rp5.get("max_scaled_diff")) + r"\le10^{-9}$).") if "WITHIN_ROUNDOFF" in _rv5 else
                 ((r"\textbf{different} in " + str(_rp5.get("n_differ")) + r" of " + str(_rp5.get("n_fields")) + r" fields --- a result, and it is stated.") if "NOT_REPRODUCED" in _rv5 else
                  (r"there was no comparison in this run (" + _tx5(_rp5.get("why") or "no record") + r")."))))
             + (r" The D128 fields were left out of the comparison: D128 did not run in this run and ran in the previous one." if _rp5.get("d128_excluded") else "")
             + r" This is computation \textsf{[COMPUTED]}; it does not move the gate.")
    s.append(r"\begin{center}\small\texttt{" + _tt5(_ax5.get("verdict") or "TGL_THE_AXIOM_V385__ABSENT") + r"}\end{center}")
